From: Cody <cody@goldberg.fyi>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: enable rear mic on ASRock 26ce:0a08

The rear microphone on the ASRock X870 Steel Legend WiFi (26ce:0a08)
enumerates and streams, but its signal is about 25 dB too quiet. The
device's UAC2 descriptors expose mute and volume controls, but not the
private widget assignment performed by the vendor driver.

ASRock also uses this USB ID for the Z790 PG-ITX/TB4; both boards are
specified with ALC4082 audio. The vendor driver's entry for this exact ID
selects the same widget-assignment path, so match the USB identity rather
than X870-specific DMI data.

Assign the rear microphone widget when preparing capture endpoint 0x83. On
the tested board after a USB reset under the stock driver, this command
increased a fixed 1 kHz acoustic signal from -69.3 to -44.5 dBFS. A
separate five-register transaction observed in the vendor driver made no
additional signal-level change and is intentionally excluded.

Use the mode-selection hook so a failed or short control transfer aborts
PCM prepare and remains retryable. Endpoint preparation reapplies the
idempotent command after close/reopen and after suspend.

The command-only module was loaded before a USB re-enumeration and fixed
the first capture prepare. It remained stable through 100 rear capture
open/prepare/close cycles, 20 front capture cycles, all four playback PCMs,
runtime and system suspend/resume, simultaneous capture/playback, and a
normal PipeWire capture, with no new USB audio warnings.

---
 sound/usb/quirks.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/quirks.c b/sound/usb/quirks.c
index eb1750def..8560c726c 100644
--- a/sound/usb/quirks.c
+++ b/sound/usb/quirks.c
@@ -1855,6 +1855,31 @@ static int rme_digiface_set_format_quirk(struct snd_usb_substream *subs)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#define ALC4082_REQ_WIDGET_COMMAND 0x6c
+
+static int alc4082_rear_capture_quirk(struct snd_usb_audio *chip)
+{
+	struct usb_device *dev = chip->dev;
+	u8 command = 0x0f;
+	int err;
+
+	/* The rear microphone assignment is not exposed through UAC. */
+	err = snd_usb_ctl_msg(dev, usb_sndctrlpipe(dev, 0),
+			      ALC4082_REQ_WIDGET_COMMAND,
+			      USB_DIR_OUT | USB_TYPE_VENDOR | USB_RECIP_DEVICE,
+			      0, 1, &command, sizeof(command));
+	if (err != sizeof(command)) {
+		if (err >= 0)
+			err = -EIO;
+		usb_audio_err(chip,
+			      "failed to activate ALC4082 rear mic: %d\n",
+			      err);
+		return err;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 void snd_usb_set_format_quirk(struct snd_usb_substream *subs,
 			      const struct audioformat *fmt)
 {
@@ -1894,6 +1919,12 @@ int snd_usb_select_mode_quirk(struct snd_usb_audio *chip,
 	struct usb_device *dev = chip->dev;
 	int err;
 
+	if (chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x26ce, 0x0a08) && fmt->endpoint == 0x83) {
+		err = alc4082_rear_capture_quirk(chip);
+		if (err < 0)
+			return err;
+	}
+
 	if (chip->quirk_flags & QUIRK_FLAG_ITF_USB_DSD_DAC) {
 		/* First switch to alt set 0, otherwise the mode switch cmd
 		 * will not be accepted by the DAC
-- 
